::error file=domain/entities.go,line=13,col=2,title=E010 remote-FK to-one relation is not guaranteed unique::domain.User.Session is orm.One but public.sessions(user_id) is not unique%0A%0Anothing stops two rows from referencing the same one, so a to-one relation would silently pick whichever came back first%0A%0AFix: add a total unique constraint on public.sessions(user_id), or declare the field as orm.Many[Session]
::error file=domain/entities.go,line=14,col=2,title=E010 remote-FK to-one relation is not guaranteed unique::domain.User.Badge is orm.One but public.badges(user_id) is not unique%0A%0Abadges_one_active_per_user is a partial unique index, so it says nothing about the rows its WHERE clause excludes; a to-one relation would silently drop rows%0A%0AFix: add a total unique constraint on public.badges(user_id), or declare the field as orm.Many[Badge]
